Choosing the right EdTech company starts with understanding the learner's goals. Compare course syllabuses, practical assignments, teaching methods, trainer experience, and student support before making a decision.

For technology courses, check whether students get opportunities to build projects, practise coding, work with robotics kits, or explore AI applications. These activities can help learners connect theoretical knowledge with practical experience.

A suitable education provider should offer a clear curriculum, appropriate guidance, and learning activities that match the student's age and skill level.

